.SH "Ajv: Another JSON Schema Validator"
.PP
The fastest JSON Schema validator for Node\&.js and browser\&. Supports draft-04/06/07\&.

.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP
.SS "Ajv v7 beta is released"
\fRAjv version 7\&.0\&.0-beta\&.0\fP is released with these changes:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
to reduce the mistakes in JSON schemas and unexpected validation results, \fBstrict mode\fP is added - it prohibits ignored or ambiguous JSON Schema elements\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
to make code injection from untrusted schemas impossible, \fBcode generation\fP is fully re-written to be safe\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
to simplify Ajv extensions, the new keyword API that is used by pre-defined keywords is available to user-defined keywords - it is much easier to define any keywords now, especially with subschemas\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
schemas are compiled to ES6 code (ES5 code generation is supported with an option)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
to improve reliability and maintainability the code is migrated to TypeScript\&.
.PP

.PP
\fBPlease note\fP:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
the support for JSON-Schema draft-04 is removed - if you have schemas using "id" attributes you have to replace them with "\\$id" (or continue using version 6 that will be supported until 02/28/2021)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
all formats are separated to ajv-formats package - they have to be explicitely added if you use them\&.
.PP

.PP
See \fRrelease notes\fP for the details\&.

.PP
To install the new version:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install ajv@beta
.fi
.PP

.PP
See \fRGetting started with v7\fP for code example\&.
